Ref-to-pointer downgrade (`&r` where `r: &T` → `*T`)
======================================================

Per CLAUDE.md's three-mode Conversion Rules:

  - `ref → ptr`: `&r` yields a raw `*T` pointing at the same
    heap allocation `r` references. **Unsafe** — no refcount
    change, no lifetime extension. If the originating ref
    drops while the raw pointer is still in use, the pointer
    dangles; the programmer owns that risk. This is the
    explicit escape hatch for handing ARC-managed data to
    kernel-style code whose API takes `*T`.

  - `ptr → ref`: ALWAYS REJECTED. You can't manufacture a
    refcount from a raw pointer. That direction lives in
    `compile_errors/compile_fail_ptr_to_ref.lsysl` (gated on
    the `compile_errors/` infrastructure).

Each test below pins one corner of the downgrade contract: a
read through `*p`, a mutation through `*p` that's visible to the
original ref, the same `r.field == p.field` value visible both
ways, and passing `*T` to a function whose signature takes a raw
pointer.

    module sysl.tests.lang_features

    struct R2pBox
        v: int
        tag: int

### Read through `*p` sees the heap value

    #test
    test_r2p_read_through_ptr() -> unit
        val r: &R2pBox = new R2pBox(42, 7)
        val p: *R2pBox = &r
        assert(p.v == 42, "v through ptr")
        assert(p.tag == 7, "tag through ptr")

### Mutation through `*p` is visible through the original ref

    #test
    test_r2p_mutate_through_ptr() -> unit
        val r: &R2pBox = new R2pBox(1, 0)
        val p: *R2pBox = &r
        p.v = 99
        p.tag = 3
        assert(r.v == 99, "mutated v visible via ref")
        assert(r.tag == 3, "mutated tag visible via ref")

### Ref and pointer coexist and see the same data

    #test
    test_r2p_coexist() -> unit
        val r: &R2pBox = new R2pBox(11, 22)
        val p: *R2pBox = &r
        assert(r.v == p.v, "v")
        assert(r.tag == p.tag, "tag")
        r.v = 33
        assert(p.v == 33, "ref mutate seen by ptr")

### Pass `*T` derived from `&T` to a `*T`-taking function

    r2p_sum_via_ptr(p: *R2pBox) -> int
        p.v + p.tag

    #test
    test_r2p_pass_as_ptr_param() -> unit
        val r: &R2pBox = new R2pBox(10, 20)
        assert(r2p_sum_via_ptr(&r) == 30, "ptr param")
